Description: tray icon for PulseAudio and PipeWire volume control
 pulse-volumeicon is a small system tray icon to control the sound volume.
 Scroll over the icon to change the volume, middle click to toggle mute,
 and left click for a menu.
 .
 It uses the StatusNotifierItem protocol, so it works in KDE Plasma, Xfce,
 Waybar and other modern trays, with a fallback for older XEmbed trays.
 The volume is changed through pactl, which also works with PipeWire.
